From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: XP's black boxes for sizes drawn with embedded bitmaps

Purpose: give text in the XP shell session XP's character widths, and so
XP's edit control margins (MS UI Gothic 9 point, the dialog font).
Windows behavior: XP draws MS UI Gothic -12 with its embedded bitmaps and
measures a glyph's black box from the bitmap's inked columns, its advance
from the outline. Of characters 0 to 255 only two have a negative A width;
a kana's C width is 1 or 2, 目 is 1/8/3 (abcw.exe and cw.exe on the
reference XP machine). An edit control's margins come from these widths
(0 and 1 pixels).
Wine before: GetCharABCWidths read the outline's box, so "f", "j", "r"
and others had negative A or C widths, every kana's C width was 0, and
an edit control's text started a pixel further right (margins 1 and 2).
Change: in the XP shell session, the black box of a glyph of a size with
embedded bitmaps is the loaded bitmap's inked columns; the advance stays
the outline's.
Evidence: abcw.exe and cw.exe give XP's values for every character
tested; the edit, list box and other controls of xpcmp.exe are
pixel-identical to XP's.
Scope: the XP shell session (WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL, no WIN4WINE_SHELL).
---
 dlls/win32u/freetype.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/freetype.c b/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
index c6a501c..8e346ac 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
@@ -3236,6 +3236,42 @@ static UINT freetype_get_glyph_outline( struct gdi_font *font, UINT glyph, UINT
     if (win4wine_external_shell() && !matrices && !vertical_metrics && FT_IS_SCALABLE( ft_face ) &&
         metrics.horiAdvance == ((((ft_face->glyph->linearHoriAdvance + 512) >> 10) + 32) & -64))
         metrics.horiAdvance = ((ft_face->glyph->linearHoriAdvance + 0x8000) >> 16) << 6;
+    /* XP measures the black box of a size that has embedded bitmaps, which it
+     * draws with them, from the bitmap, and the advance from the outline:
+     * MS UI Gothic -12's "f" and "j" have no negative A or C width there and
+     * its kana have a C width (abcw.exe and cw.exe on the reference XP
+     * machine); an edit control's margins come from these. */
+    if (format == GGO_METRICS && !matrices && !vertical_metrics && !(load_flags & FT_LOAD_NO_HINTING) &&
+        !font->fake_bold && has_bitmap_strike( font ) && win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP &&
+        !pFT_Load_Glyph( ft_face, glyph, get_load_flags( GGO_BITMAP ) ) &&
+        ft_face->glyph->format == FT_GLYPH_FORMAT_BITMAP)
+    {
+        const FT_Bitmap *bitmap = &ft_face->glyph->bitmap;
+        FT_Pos advance = metrics.horiAdvance;
+        int x, y, first = bitmap->width, last = -1;
+
+        metrics = ft_face->glyph->metrics;
+        metrics.horiAdvance = advance;
+        /* the inked columns: a kanji's bitmap is as wide as the em (目 is 1/8/3) */
+        if (bitmap->pixel_mode == FT_PIXEL_MODE_MONO || bitmap->pixel_mode == FT_PIXEL_MODE_GRAY)
+        {
+            for (y = 0; y < (int)bitmap->rows; y++)
+            {
+                const unsigned char *row = bitmap->buffer + y * bitmap->pitch;
+                for (x = 0; x < (int)bitmap->width; x++)
+                    if (bitmap->pixel_mode == FT_PIXEL_MODE_MONO ? row[x >> 3] & (0x80 >> (x & 7)) : row[x])
+                    {
+                        first = min( first, x );
+                        last = max( last, x );
+                    }
+            }
+            if (last >= first)
+            {
+                metrics.horiBearingX += first << 6;
+                metrics.width = (last - first + 1) << 6;
+            }
+        }
+    }
     if(font->fake_bold) {
         if (!get_bold_glyph_outline(ft_face->glyph, font->ppem, &metrics) && metrics.width)
             metrics.width += 1 << 6;
